Music School Management System (MSMS) Overview
The Music School Management System (MSMS) is a lightweight, in-memory Python application designed to manage the daily operations of a music school. Through a simple command-line interface (CLI), it enables front desk staff to register students, schedule instrument lessons, and query information about students and teachers.

Features
Student Management: Register new students and track their course enrollments.
Teacher Management: Maintain a database of teachers and their areas of expertise.
Search Functionality: Quickly locate students or teachers using keywords (case-insensitive).
Course Registration: Easily add new instrument courses for existing students.
Administrator Tools: View complete lists of all registered students and teachers in the system.

Getting Started
Prerequisites
Python 3.x must be installed on your machine.

How to Run
Clone or download the repository to your local machine.
Open a terminal or command prompt.
Navigate to the directory containing MSMS.py.
Run the program using the following command: Bash
python MSMS.py Usage
After running the program, you will see a menu. Simply enter the corresponding number or letter for the action you wish to perform:

Register New Student: Create a student profile and enroll them in an instrument.
Enrol Existing Student: Use the student's ID to add a new instrument course to their existing record.
Lookup Student or Teacher: Enter a name or specialty/instrument to search and locate any records.
List all Students: Display summary information for each student in the database.
List all Teachers: Display summary information for each teacher in the database.
q. Quit: Safely exit the application.

Project Structure
MSMS.py: Main source code containing logic, data models, and interactive menu.

